    <!-- Plant descriptions -->
    <string name="plant_tulip_desc">An elegant spring flower symbolizing love and rebirth. It is often one of the first signs that winter is ending.</string>
    <string name="plant_poppy_desc">A delicate wildflower symbolizing memories and peace. It grows freely in meadows and along roads, softening the landscape.</string>
    <string name="plant_sunflower_desc">A sunny giant that always follows the light. Its large blooms can reach impressive sizes and dominate any garden.</string>
    <string name="plant_daffodil_desc">A herald of spring with a bright and cheerful fragrance. Its yellow blooms often appear before the snow has fully melted.</string>
    <string name="plant_rose_desc">The queen of flowers, symbolizing love and beauty. It comes in many varieties and colors, each carrying its own meaning.</string>
    <string name="plant_bloodroot_desc">A rare forest flower that blooms for only a few days. Its delicate petals emerge very early in spring.</string>
    <string name="plant_gerbera_desc">A colorful and joyful flower symbolizing enthusiasm and happiness. It is often used in bouquets thanks to its durability and vivid colors.</string>
    <string name="plant_pansy_desc">A small flower with velvety petals and cheerful colors. It is cold-resistant and often blooms even in early spring.</string>
    <string name="plant_lavender_desc">An aromatic plant known for its calming and relaxing effects. Its scent is widely used in cosmetics and aromatherapy.</string>
    <string name="plant_lily_desc">A majestic flower symbolizing purity and innocence. Its large, elegant petals make it popular for ceremonial occasions.</string>
    <string name="plant_orchid_desc">An exotic beauty and one of the most refined plants in the world. It requires specific conditions but rewards with stunning blooms.</string>

